body:
So, this PR is far from done and in need of code reviews, so thanks.

I'm intending to extend it to `SpringBoneCollisionCapsule` shape when I have the time.  (Though I should be focusing on the audio system for godotcon in Amsterdam.)  

The calculation has an instability when the contact point is close to the base of the cone and the leverage is high which causes the spring to twitch wildly.  I have suppressed the contact in that part of the cone, but I'd like to do more work to make it more stable.

There's also a question whether more of the pre-calculations should be moved into `SpringBone3DVerletInfo` (which already contains the `bone_length`).  Specifically the gradient slope of the cone, given by:

```C++
float taper_fore = (p_bone_origin_radius - p_bone_radius) / p_bone_length;
float taper_side = sqrt(1.0 - taper_fore * taper_fore);
float cone_gradient = taper_fore / taper_side;
```

Are values put into this struct available to the visualizer in terms of over-drawing the cone gizmo in the right place on the sphere gizmos?
